run, those pirates are finished.

260
00:14:12,620 --> 00:14:14,437
What the hell's going on here?

261
00:14:14,520 --> 00:14:16,917
Don't tell me this is the same beach.

262
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:19,960
I don't have time for this crap right now.

263
00:14:29,760 --> 00:14:30,980
Now, hold on, sir.

264
00:14:31,260 --> 00:14:33,157
The only person here is our president, Mr.

265
00:14:33,240 --> 00:14:34,070
Iceberg.

266
00:14:34,760 --> 00:14:36,977
Toobin, I know you're
hiding those pirates.

267
00:14:37,060 --> 00:14:38,157
I swear, we're not.

268
00:14:38,240 --> 00:14:39,697
Hey, you can't go inside.

269
00:14:39,780 --> 00:14:40,610
Hold on.

270
00:14:40,693 --> 00:14:41,717
The Straw Hats are heroes.

271
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:42,630
Hey, shut up.

272
00:14:56,960 --> 00:14:58,880
All right, you two. Wait here.

273
00:14:59,520 --> 00:15:00,350
Yes, sir!

274
00:15:05,240 --> 00:15:06,300
What the hell?

275
00:15:06,540 --> 00:15:07,500
What's going on?

276
00:15:12,640 --> 00:15:16,040
Pardon me, but are you
folks the Straw Hat Pirates?

277
00:15:16,400 --> 00:15:21,077
You see, I have some friends here that
would like to share our word with Monkey D.

278
00:15:21,160 --> 00:15:21,990
Luffy.

279
00:15:22,073 --> 00:15:22,903
The Navy!

280
00:15:25,020 --> 00:15:26,200
Rise and shine!

281
00:15:33,880 --> 00:15:34,710
Ow!

282
00:15:34,793 --> 00:15:35,623
That hurt!

283
00:15:36,440 --> 00:15:37,340
What happened?

284
00:15:37,540 --> 00:15:39,577
Why would one little
punch hurt you so much?

285
00:15:39,660 --> 00:15:40,837
You're made of rubber!

286
00:15:40,920 --> 00:15:44,760
It's because there is no
defense against a fist of love.

287
00:15:45,160 --> 00:15:48,377
You've been getting in a lot
of trouble lately, haven't you?

288
00:15:48,460 --> 00:15:49,290
Luffy.

289
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:52,830
Grandpa?

290
00:16:02,080 --> 00:16:03,240
It's been a while.

291
00:16:06,200 --> 00:16:08,557
I think you owe me an apology, boy!

292
00:16:08,640 --> 00:16:10,437
You've been up to no good.

293
00:16:10,520 --> 00:16:14,755
But isn't that the name of the Navy
hero that fought against Gold Roger?

294
00:16:14,840 --> 00:16:18,340
Luffy, is this Navy guy
really your grandpa? Sure is!

295
00:16:18,560 --> 00:16:20,597
No matter what, don't try to fight him!

296
00:16:20,680 --> 00:16:25,209
He'll kill you just like he almost killed
me over and over when I was little.

297
00:16:35,600 --> 00:16:38,397
Now, now, you're gonna
give them the wrong idea,

298
00:16:38,480 --> 00:16:43,660
although I admit I did throw
you into a ravine that one time,

299
00:16:43,800 --> 00:16:48,400
and I left you in the
jungle a few times too,

300
00:16:48,740 --> 00:16:54,100
and sure there were those times I
sent you sailing on those balloons,

301
00:16:54,460 --> 00:16:59,777
but I didn't do it to kill you,
I did it to make you a man.

302
00:16:59,860 --> 00:17:00,690
I

303
00:17:00,773 --> 00:17:07,740
see.

304
00:17:09,360 --> 00:17:12,257
So this is where all of
Luffy's endurance comes from.

305
00:17:12,340 --> 00:17:14,917
This is why everything
rolls off of him when

306
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:17,057
I left you and Ace with
my friend for training.

307
00:17:17,140 --> 00:17:18,977
I thought everything would work out fine,

308
00:17:19,060 --> 00:17:24,997
but I turned my back

309
00:17:25,080 --> 00:17:26,377
and you end up like this.

310
00:17:26,460 --> 00:17:28,917
I wanted to make you into a navy man.

311
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:29,897
You stinking ingrate.

312
00:17:29,980 --> 00:17:31,417
How the heck did you become a criminal?

313
00:17:31,500 --> 00:17:33,237
I told you a million times.

314
00:17:33,320 --> 00:17:34,317
I wanted to be a pirate.

315
00:17:34,400 --> 00:17:35,797
It's not my fault you wouldn't listen.

316
00:17:35,880 --> 00:17:37,857
This is all that damn redhead's fault.

317
00:17:37,940 --> 00:17:39,457
The fool. I.

318
00:17:39,540 --> 00:17:42,197
I wouldn't even be alive
if it wasn't for Sexy.

319
00:17:42,280 --> 00:17:43,257
Shut up.

320
00:17:43,340 --> 00:17:46,177
Shut up. Huh?

321
00:17:46,260 --> 00:17:47,937
Is that any way to speak to your grandpa?

322
00:17:48,020 --> 00:17:48,897
Oh right.

323
00:17:48,980 --> 00:17:49,957
I'm sorry.

324
00:17:50,040 --> 00:17:51,240
We're all set for!

325
00:17:51,420 --> 00:17:53,457
A captain's been captured by the Marines!

326
00:17:53,540 --> 00:17:54,370
Luffy!

327
00:17:55,840 --> 00:17:57,577
Help! No! This is bad.

328
00:17:57,660 --> 00:17:58,937
If we try to help Luffy,

329
00:17:59,020 --> 00:18:02,902
then all those Marines outside are
going to rush in and attack us!

330
00:18:05,660 --> 00:18:06,601
They're asleep?!

331
00:18:07,720 --> 00:18:10,480
So wait, what are we supposed to do here?

332
00:18:10,760 --> 00:18:13,584
I've never been in a
situation like this before.

333
00:18:14,780 --> 00:18:16,604
Oh no, did I fall asleep again?

334
00:18:20,160 --> 00:18:22,117
Wake up and take your lecture like a man!

335
00:18:22,200 --> 00:18:25,640
Don't you dare goes off on
me when I'm yelling at you?

336
00:18:42,660 --> 00:18:44,013
That's his grandfather.

337
00:18:44,460 --> 00:18:47,237
Well, it's no wonder Luffy
never talked about his family.

338
00:18:47,320 --> 00:18:48,520
This is crazy

339
00:18:54,600 --> 00:18:57,197
Speaking of that red-headed
pirate friend of yours,

340
00:18:57,280 --> 00:19:00,577
do you have any clue what kind of
dangerous business he's involved in?

341
00:19:00,660 --> 00:19:04,013
No, I haven't heard anything
about Shanks in a long time.

342
00:19:04,220 --> 00:19:06,120
Is he okay? What's he up to?

343
00:19:06,460 --> 00:19:08,120
Is he okay? Of course.

344
00:19:09,040 --> 00:19:12,517
There's as many pirates out there
as there are stars in the sky.

345
00:19:12,600 --> 00:19:14,777
But that redhead's one of the brightest.

346
00:19:14,860 --> 00:19:17,389
He's in the same class
as Whitebeard, even.

347
00:19:17,480 --> 00:19:20,237
There are only four pirates
as powerful as that,

348
00:19:20,320 --> 00:19:24,117
and they rule over the second half
of the Grand Line, like kings!

349
00:19:24,200 --> 00:19:25,840
They're the four emperors!

350
00:19:26,380 --> 00:19:30,600
The seven warlords and us folks of
the navy have allied against them.

351
00:19:30,760 --> 00:19:33,480
The idea is to create a balance of power.

352
00:19:34,200 --> 00:19:37,517
If any one of these three forces
grew stronger than the others,

353
00:19:37,600 --> 00:19:41,718
then the peace we worked so hard to
protect would come crumbling down.

354
00:19:44,160 --> 00:19:47,020
I don't really get it,
but I'm glad he's okay.

355
00:19:47,980 --> 00:19:49,900
Man, brings back memories, huh?

356
00:19:51,740 --> 00:19:54,269
Luffy has connections
to red-haired Shanks?

357
00:19:54,680 --> 00:19:56,974
That's where he got his Straw Hat from.

358
00:19:57,180 --> 00:19:59,298
Shanks asked him to take care of it.

359
00:19:59,520 --> 00:20:02,520
I had no idea he was such
an important guy, though.

360
00:20:06,180 --> 00:20:07,480
It's over here, Zoro!

361
00:20:08,980 --> 00:20:10,392
Damn it, we're too late!

362
00:20:10,900 --> 00:20:12,782
Anyway, good luck with the Navy.

363
00:20:13,960 --> 00:20:15,380
I'm sorry again.

364
00:20:15,800 --> 00:20:17,617
We shouldn't have tried to mug you.

365
00:20:17,700 --> 00:20:18,818
That was a mistake.

366
00:20:18,940 --> 00:20:19,977
Don't worry about it.

367
00:20:20,060 --> 00:20:21,657
Thanks for showing me the way here.

368
00:20:21,740 --> 00:20:22,570
See ya.

369
00:20:26,140 --> 00:20:27,669
What's going on out there?

370
00:20:30,040 --> 00:20:31,393
It's the pirate hunter.

371
00:20:31,580 --> 00:20:34,227
He seems to be going on
some sort of rampage.

372
00:20:34,780 --> 00:20:36,427
He's from Luffy's crew, huh?

373
00:20:36,880 --> 00:20:38,240
He looks pretty tough.

374
00:20:39,080 --> 00:20:40,217
Go ahead, you two.

375
00:20:40,300 --> 00:20:42,060
Give him hell, sir

376
00:20:52,120 --> 00:20:53,300
Cookery knives, huh?

377
00:20:53,520 --> 00:20:54,917
Interesting choice of a weapon.

378
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:55,941
You've got there

379
00:21:01,980 --> 00:21:03,580
For you, Jack?

380
00:21:20,080 --> 00:21:21,157
Are you okay?

381
00:21:21,240 --> 00:21:25,457
What happened, boys?

382
00:21:25,540 --> 00:21:26,957
You're no match at all.

383
00:21:27,040 --> 00:21:29,277
You're as tough as I thought you'd be.

384
00:21:29,360 --> 00:21:33,017
That was a nice one, anyway.

385
00:21:33,100 --> 00:21:33,940
I give...

386
00:21:37,560 --> 00:21:39,160
Hi, Luffy. Hi, Zoro.

387
00:21:40,440 --> 00:21:41,499
It's been a while.

388
00:21:41,780 --> 00:21:43,015
Do you know who I am?

389
00:21:44,500 --> 00:21:45,500
Uh, no.

390
00:21:46,060 --> 00:21:48,040
Look, it's me. It's Kobe.

391
00:21:48,760 --> 00:21:50,584
You mean you don't remember me?

392
00:21:54,960 --> 00:21:55,820
Kobe, huh?

393
00:21:57,180 --> 00:21:59,140
I do have a friend named Kobe.

394
00:21:59,400 --> 00:22:02,337
But the Kobe I know is a
whole lot smaller than you.

395
00:22:02,420 --> 00:22:03,250
Sorry.

396
00:22:03,400 --> 00:22:05,120
Nope, that's the right Kobe.

397
00:22:05,360 --> 00:22:08,125
The crybaby, good-for-nothing
Kobe from before.

398
00:22:09,540 --> 00:22:10,420
No way!

399
00:22:11,720 --> 00:22:12,780
Yeah, that's him.

400
00:22:13,400 --> 00:22:15,237
But why is he on the Grand Line?

401
00:22:15,320 --> 00:22:18,157
To be honest, I'm not a
commissioned Navy officer yet.

402
00:22:18,240 --> 00:22:20,317
But when I heard you
guys were in the area,

403
00:22:20,400 --> 00:22:23,929
I had to stop by and say hello
while I still had the chance.

404
00:22:26,500 --> 00:22:30,180
If it wasn't for you two, we
wouldn't be where we are today.

405
00:22:31,240 --> 00:22:32,070
Hmph.

406
00:22:32,153 --> 00:22:34,100
Well, I wouldn't go quite that far.

407
00:22:34,480 --> 00:22:37,200
A lot of stuff happened,
but long story short,

408
00:22:37,400 --> 00:22:40,237
we ended up being trained by
Vice Admiral Garp himself.

409
00:22:40,320 --> 00:22:41,840
Must have been hard work!

410
00:22:42,420 --> 00:22:46,300
Man, you grew so much from before,
I didn't even recognize you!

411
00:22:46,420 --> 00:22:47,300
It's crazy!

412
00:22:47,780 --> 00:22:50,680
The Kobe I remember was
a pudgy little dorky guy!

413
00:22:51,140 --> 00:22:53,497
I'm sure you're worn out
after all that happened.

414
00:22:53,580 --> 00:22:54,410
Sorry to bother you.

415
00:22:54,493 --> 00:22:55,480
Nah, it's fine!

416
00:22:55,660 --> 00:22:57,237
I haven't seen you in ages!

417
00:22:57,320 --> 00:22:58,520
We gotta celebrate!

418
00:22:59,280 --> 00:23:00,620
Hey, you bastards!

419
00:23:01,000 --> 00:23:02,000
Hold on a second!

420
00:23:02,240 --> 00:23:05,000
You didn't recognize me at all, huh?

421
00:23:05,360 --> 00:23:06,940
Who the hell are you?

422
00:23:07,260 --> 00:23:10,540
It's me! See? Me!

423
00:23:11,000 --> 00:23:13,160
No, I don't see. Just tell me.

424
00:23:13,900 --> 00:23:15,440
Get a clue, guys.

425
00:23:17,700 --> 00:23:21,740
It's Helmepo, Captain
Morgan's son, Helmepo.

426
00:23:22,440 --> 00:23:24,217
Surely you remember now.

427
00:23:24,300 --> 00:23:28,780
I had you tied up you were almost
executed because of me Zoro.

428
00:23:29,020 --> 00:23:31,549
You couldn't possibly
forget that could you

429
00:23:34,680 --> 00:23:35,877
Really guys?

430
00:23:35,960 --> 00:23:38,040
Stop giving me such a hard time!

431
00:23:39,800 --> 00:23:41,280
No one likes a bully.

432
00:23:43,060 --> 00:23:46,820
Zoro you seem to be handling
this well, don't you agree?

433
00:23:47,480 --> 00:23:48,620
No, stop!

434
00:23:48,840 --> 00:23:50,420
I worked so hard!

435
00:23:50,700 --> 00:23:51,917
I made empty threats?

436
00:23:52,000 --> 00:23:54,118
I was always talking about my daddy?

437
00:23:56,820 --> 00:23:58,380
Oh, that guy.

438
00:23:58,920 --> 00:24:00,508
What do you mean, that guy?

439
00:24:01,640 --> 00:24:02,737
Yeah, right.

440
00:24:02,820 --> 00:24:03,940
You sucked.

441
00:24:04,160 --> 00:24:05,360
No wonder I forgot.

442
00:24:06,140 --> 00:24:09,860
I wanted to forgive
them, but I just can't.

443
00:24:09,980 --> 00:24:11,360
I'm so sorry, Koby.

444
00:24:11,620 --> 00:24:14,677
You just have to accept the
past and move on, Helmepo.

445
00:24:14,760 --> 00:24:15,957
He still sucks.

446
00:24:16,040 --> 00:24:17,220
Looks like it.

447
00:24:17,500 --> 00:24:21,560
Now, I've got a job for
you boys. Sir! This wall?

448
00:24:21,920 --> 00:24:24,700
Fix it. What? Are you kidding?

449
00:24:25,260 --> 00:24:28,817
If you were going to have us fix it,
why'd you break it in the first place?

450
00:24:28,900 --> 00:24:31,797
Because walking through a door
doesn't make much of an impression.

451
00:24:31,880 --> 00:24:34,477
The only impression you're
making here is a bad one.

452
00:24:34,560 --> 00:24:37,637
Okay, we'll fix the wall, but it's
your fault, so you've got to help us.

453
00:24:37,720 --> 00:24:38,550
What?

454
00:24:39,140 --> 00:24:39,970
All right.

455
00:24:42,400 --> 00:24:46,580
So this grandpa of yours
is really famous. Beats me.

456
00:24:46,880 --> 00:24:49,174
I never really asked him about his job.

457
00:24:49,780 --> 00:24:55,420
By the way, Luffy, I heard you met
your old man a while back. Huh? My dad?

458
00:24:55,880 --> 00:24:57,380
No, I don't think so.

459
00:24:57,640 --> 00:24:59,700
I didn't even think I had a dad.

460
00:25:00,280 --> 00:25:01,220
That's a shame.

461
00:25:01,660 --> 00:25:04,013
I thought he'd introduce himself to you.

462
00:25:04,560 --> 00:25:07,501
From what I hear, he saw
you off back at Loguetown.

463
00:25:08,100 --> 00:25:12,041
I remember what happened, but I
sure don't remember Luffy's father.

464
00:25:12,940 --> 00:25:14,897
Uh, could you give me a hint here?

465
00:25:14,980 --> 00:25:16,140
What's dad like?

466
00:25:16,820 --> 00:25:20,640
The name of your father is Monkey D.

467
00:25:20,860 --> 00:25:22,700
Dragon, the revolutionary.

468
00:25:23,980 --> 00:25:24,980
Dragon, huh?

469
00:25:35,040 --> 00:25:36,320
That dragon?

470
00:25:36,500 --> 00:25:38,357
The revolutionary has a son?

471
00:25:38,440 --> 00:25:41,240
Even though he's famous,
Luffy didn't know.

472
00:25:42,140 --> 00:25:44,720
Wait, Dragon is Vice Admiral Garp's son?

473
00:25:44,980 --> 00:25:47,921
What kind of crazy messed
up family have they got?

474
00:25:48,040 --> 00:25:51,337
Come to think of it, I never
heard Dragon's full name before.

475
00:25:51,420 --> 00:25:52,837
What's the deal, you guys?

476
00:25:52,920 --> 00:25:54,717
Why is everyone freaking out so much?

477
00:25:54,800 --> 00:25:55,637
Are you kidding?

478
00:25:55,720 --> 00:25:58,717
You're trying to tell me you've
never heard of Dragon before?

479
00:25:58,800 --> 00:26:00,340
He's a dangerous man.

480
00:26:00,560 --> 00:26:02,080
Like, really dangerous.

481
00:26:06,460 --> 00:26:07,417
Um, Robin?

482
00:26:07,500 --> 00:26:10,577
I'm not exactly sure how
I should explain this one.

483
00:26:10,660 --> 00:26:14,837
Pirates like us are
enemies with the navy but.

484
00:26:14,920 --> 00:26:19,397
We don't usually attack them on
our own but there is one group

485
00:26:19,480 --> 00:26:22,037
that is directly opposing the
authority of the world government.

486
00:26:22,120 --> 00:26:27,617
The revolutionary army and the man
at the head of that group is Dragon.

487
00:26:27,700 --> 00:26:32,580
By now his ideology has spread to many
nations causing worldwide rebellion.

488
00:26:33,140 --> 00:26:37,081
The government's hold has already
collapsed in a number of regions.

489
00:26:37,480 --> 00:26:39,656
Naturally, the government is furious.

490
00:26:39,860 --> 00:26:42,097
They've labeled Dragon as
the world's worst criminal

491
00:26:42,180 --> 00:26:45,298
and will stop at absolutely
nothing to hunt him down.

492
00:26:45,780 --> 00:26:48,997
The problem is that no one
knows a single thing about him.

493
00:26:49,080 --> 00:26:50,700
He's very mysterious.

494
00:26:51,860 --> 00:26:52,817
And yet...

495
00:26:52,900 --> 00:26:54,000
And yet what?

496
00:26:55,900 --> 00:26:58,180
Uh, that was a mistake, huh?

497
00:26:58,440 --> 00:27:01,146
I probably shouldn't
have said all that stuff.

498
00:27:04,500 --> 00:27:06,100
I take it all back.

499
00:27:06,320 --> 00:27:07,620
Forget it, okay?

500
00:27:14,040 --> 00:27:14,870
What?
